<div class="headline-area"><div class="headlines">	<h1 class="entry-title ">

	
				<span class="dfm-title metered">
			RETURN OF CIVIL WAR VA. FLAG IS SOUGHT		</span>



	
	
	</h1>
</div></div><div class="article-share" id="sharing-top"><div class="sharedaddy sd-sharing-enabled"><div class="robots-nocontent sd-block sd-social sd-social-icon sd-sharing"><h3 class="sd-title">Share this:</h3><div class="sd-content"><ul><li class="share-facebook"><a rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer"
				data-shared="sharing-facebook-1958190"
				class="share-facebook sd-button share-icon no-text"
				href="https://www.pilotonline.com/2000/02/11/return-of-civil-war-va-flag-is-sought/?share=facebook"
				target="_blank"
				aria-labelledby="sharing-facebook-1958190-4"
				>
				<span id="sharing-facebook-1958190-4" hidden>Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)</span>
				<span>Facebook</span>
			</a></li><li class="share-x"><a rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer"
				data-shared="sharing-x-1958190"
				class="share-x sd-button share-icon no-text"
				href="https://www.pilotonline.com/2000/02/11/return-of-civil-war-va-flag-is-sought/?share=x"
				target="_blank"
				aria-labelledby="sharing-x-1958190-4"
				>
				<span id="sharing-x-1958190-4" hidden>Share on X (Opens in new window)</span>
				<span>X</span>
			</a></li><li class="share-end"></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></header><div class="article-content"><div class="article-content-wrapper article-content-two-column"><div class="header-features"><div class="dfm-featured-top-flex-container"></div><div class="meta"><img alt='Author' src='https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/?s=85&#038;d=mm&#038;r=g' srcset='https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/?s=170&#038;d=mm&#038;r=g 2x' class='avatar avatar-85 photo avatar-default coauthor-avatar' height='85' width='85' /><div class="coauthor-avatar-container"><div class="byline">By <a href="https://www.pilotonline.com/author/the-washington-post/" title="Posts by The Washington Post" class=" author-name" aria-label="Author: The Washington Post" rel="author">The Washington Post</a></div><div class="time">PUBLISHED: <time datetime="2000-02-11 00:00:00">February 11, 2000 at 12:00 AM EST</time> | UPDATED: <time datetime="2019-08-16 14:14:50">August 16, 2019 at 6:14 PM EDT</time></div></div></div></div><div class="article-body"><div class="trinity-tts-pb" dir="ltr" style="font: 12px / 18px Verdana, Arial;height: 80px;line-height: 80px;text-align: left;margin: 0 0 0 82px"><strong style="font-weight: 400">Getting your <a href="//trinityaudio.ai" style="color: #4b4a4a;text-decoration: none;font-weight: 700">Trinity Audio</a> player ready...</strong></div><div class="body-copy"><p>During Pickett&#8217;s charge &#8211; the futile final Confederate assault in the 1863 Battle of Gettysburg &#8211; a bloodied and battered flag from a decimated Virginia infantry group was seized by a Minnesota private, who claimed the souvenir as a spoil of war.</p>
<p>One hundred 37 years later, Virginians are mounting another charge &#8211; albeit a far more civil one &#8211; to get the flag back.</p>
<p>Spurred by the fervor of a Roanoke re-enactors group, state senators from Southwestern Virginia have put forth a resolution asking Minnesota to return the flag to its southern home.</p>
<p>&#8220;It&#8217;s a matter of state pride,&#8221; said Sen. John Edwards, D-Roanoke and a sponsor of the resolution. &#8220;Minnesota has refused to return the flag, and they ought to. I don&#8217;t know why they need it.&#8221;</p><div class="s2nPlayer k-9c2tt1oP" data-type="float" data-s2n-api="dfm_stn_player_script_id_9c2tt1oP"></div><script>	function dfm_stn_player_script_id_9c2tt1oP( getS2NApiForPlayer ) {
		if( typeof window.MNGAuthentication !== 'undefined' ){
			const s2nApi = getS2NApiForPlayer( document.querySelector('.k-9c2tt1oP') );
			s2nApi.float =  ! window.MNGAuthentication.isUserSubscriber();
		}
	}</script>

<p>Minnesota officials say they need the flag for the same reason that Virginia wants it: as an important reminder of their state&#8217;s role in the Civil War.</p>
<p>&#8220;Is it more important to Virginia than Minnesota? I don&#8217;t think so,&#8221; said Ian Stewart, deputy director of the Minnesota Historical Society, which has the flag. &#8220;Unless there&#8217;s a compelling legal reason to return it, we are not inclined to do so.&#8221;</p>
<p>The Virginia resolution was forwarded Monday to the full Senate by the Rules Committee. It requests that Minnesota Gov. Jesse Ventura and other state officials urge the society, which gets state money, to return the flag.</p>
<p>But Ventura is unlikely to go along because he supports the society&#8217;s stance, spokesman Paul Moore said.</p>				<div class="dfp-ad dfp-outstream_video" id="div-gpt-ad-outstream_video" style="visibility:hidden">
					<div class="htlad-outstream_video" data-unit='pilotonline.com/news/outstream_video' data-targeting=''></div>
				</div>
<p>The Senate bill isn&#8217;t the first attempt by Virginians to recapture the flag. In 1960, before the Civil War centennial, the Virginia Historical Society asked for the flag, but the Minnesota Historical Society denied the request.</p>
<p>The cause was rekindled in 1998, before the 135th anniversary of the Battle of Gettysburg, by the 28th Virginia Infantry Regiment. That&#8217;s a Roanoke re- enactment group made up largely of ancestors of the original division.</p>
<p>&#8220;This is a major affront to us,&#8221; said Chris Caveness, executive director of the 28th Virginia Infantry Regiment.</p>
<p>The flag and the private who grabbed it, Marshall Sherman, were two lucky survivors of the bloody Pennsylvania clash between the soldiers from Virginia and Minnesota.</p>				<div class="dfp-ad dfp-cube_article" id="div-gpt-ad-cube_article" style="visibility:hidden">
					<div class="htlad-cube_article" data-unit='pilotonline.com/news/cube_article' data-targeting=''></div>
				</div>
<p>Casualties were in the 80 percent range for the North and about 90 percent for the South.</p>
			</div></div><div class="article-bottom-share"><div class="article-share" id="sharing-bottom" ><div class="sharedaddy sd-sharing-enabled"><div class="robots-nocontent sd-block sd-social sd-social-icon sd-sharing"><h3 class="sd-title">Share this:</h3><div class="sd-content"><ul><li class="share-facebook"><a rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer"
